## Context

What is true that makes this worth doing now. Link to the documents that explain the
system rather than restating them.

## Approach

The shape of the change. Enough that somebody could disagree with it before the work
starts, which is the entire point of writing it down.

## Acceptance criteria

- Each one checkable by somebody who did not write the code.
- Name the command, the behaviour, or the artifact that settles it.
- "Works correctly" is not a criterion. "`ilk check` passes and the new gate fails a
  repository with an unresolved conflict" is.

## Out of scope

What a reasonable reader might assume is included and is not.
